    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Augustin Lignier is a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "professional",
            "ref": "v-professional"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " photographer in Paris. While he was in graduate school"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "研究生院"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", one question kept bugging him: Why do so many people like to photograph their lives and share "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " online? Lignier wasn’t the first "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2,
            "hint": {
              "baseWord": "ask"
            }
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " this question, but it led him to an unexpected place. Before long, he found himself "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3,
            "hint": {
              "baseWord": "build"
            }
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a photo booth"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "自助快照亭"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for two rats."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Lignier got the idea from the famous psychologist B.F. Skinner and his Skinner box. The device gave the lab rats inside food whenever they pressed a button. Over time, the rats "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4,
            "hint": {
              "baseWord": "become"
            }
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " button-pressing pros. They pressed the button over and over again for their next "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "treat",
            "ref": "v-treat"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Lignier created his own “Skinner box”. It was a tall, transparent"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "透明的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " tower "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a simple button. Inside, he placed two pet-store rats. Each time a rat pressed the button, it got a bit of sugar, and a camera outside the tower took its photo. The pictures were immediately displayed to the rats, "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Lignier thinks they couldn’t understand them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The rats quickly became excited about pressing the button. But "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a period of training, Lignier changed the rules. Although the rats were still photographed whenever they pressed the button, the sweet treats came only "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "occasionally",
            "ref": "v-occasionally"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8,
            "hint": {
              "baseWord": "surprise"
            }
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", the rats didn’t seem to mind. They continued to enjoy pressing the button. Sometimes they even turned a blind eye to the sugar when it arrived."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "This finding brought Lignier back to his question. In many ways, social media is just "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a Skinner box for the modern human. The "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "rewards",
            "ref": "v-reward"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "—likes or new followers—are unpredictable, yet they keep us taking and posting new pictures. It seems we have "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10,
            "hint": {
              "baseWord": "much"
            }
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in common with rats than we’d like to admit!"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
